        "procedure": "At room temperature, 0.20 mmol portions of Yb(OAc)3·4H2O (0.0700 g), Zn(OAc)2·2H2O (0.0367 g), and H2L (0.1104 g) were dissolved in 20 mL of methanol. Then 1.0 mol/L trimethylamine in 1 mL of ethanol was added. The mixture was heated for 3 h with stirring under reflux, cooled to room temperature, and filtered. Slow diffusion of diethyl ether into the clear solution for 1 week produced a red crystalline solid. Syntheses of the lanthanide complexes were carried out using Schlenk techniques.",
