      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "In CH3CN, hexanuclear 2 shows Yb(III) NIR emission at 980 and 1022 nm (τ = 13.62 μs, Φem = 0.21%, estimated ΦLn = 0.68%, ligand-to-Yb sensitization efficiency 30.9%). It functions as a NIR luminescent sensor for fluoroquinolone antibiotics via inner-filter quenching at 980 nm, with KSV = 1.5×10^5 M^-1 and LOD = 0.18 μM for ciprofloxacin (CPFX) and KSV = 7.6×10^4 M^-1 and LOD = 0.36 μM for norfloxacin (NFX); other tested antibiotics quench much more weakly and do not change the CPFX/NFX response.",
